{"availability":"available","full":"arun3676/code-tribunal","name":"code-tribunal","description":"Did the AI build what you asked? Multi-agent intent-conformance review for AI-generated code — CLI, MCP server, live courtroom demo","category":"Developer tools","language":"Python","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-06-18T09:39:56Z","updated":"2026-08-01T07:58:29Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://code-council.vercel.app","topics":["ai","cli","code-quality","code-review","developer-tools","fastapi","llm","mcp","mcp-server","nextjs"],"demo":"https://code-council.vercel.app/","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T18:23:23.415Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-08T18:23:23.415Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-08T18:23:23.415Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-08T18:23:23.415Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":["Next.js","Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Did the AI build what you actually asked for?","Code Tribunal is an intent-conformance review engine for AI-generated code. Instead of asking one model whether a diff looks correct, Tribunal reconciles the original ticket against the actual implementation and returns a merge verdict, a 0–100 trust score, and a traceability ledger.","A CLERK agent opens the case. ADVOCATE extracts requirements. SURVEYOR inspects the diff. GHOST finds requested work that is missing. DRIFT finds unrequested scope changes. WARDEN is recruited for security-sensitive changes. ARBITER produces the verdict."],"features":["CLI — tribunal verify in any terminal or CI pipeline (exit 0 = APPROVE, 1 = BLOCK).","MCP server — drop it into Claude Code, Codex, or Cursor so your coding agent can self-check a diff before a human ever sees it.","Web demo — a live War Room that shows the agents deliberating: code-council.vercel.app."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/arun3676/code-tribunal/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"619c6602afd981a814078f274f3d3411140f956ea44dadf789d56021b7ef70c7","extractedAt